hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1602","Narrated to us Hārūn ibn Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Fuḍayl, on the authority of al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful, on the authority of Anas ibn Mālik (RA), who said:
One day, the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) was leading the prayer, then he finished and turned to face us. He said:
“O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, nor in sitting, nor in turning away. For I see you from behind me. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you could see what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much.”

They said: “O Messenger of Allāh, what did you see?”
He said: “I saw Paradise and the Fire.”

**CHAPTER:**"
